{"type":"text","timestamp":1788384294461,"sessionID":"ses_f9bffbda6ffeJ1dcm6DAgrG4UR","part":{"id":"prt_06402a819001ygSLgkjJjMffv9","messageID":"msg_06402a115001I2pCQ33WnJrYPk","sessionID":"ses_f9bffbda6ffeJ1dcm6DAgrG4UR","type":"text","text":"Everything is implemented and passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nCreated a Go REST API for book management in `/workspace`:\n\n- **`go.mod`** — module using pure-Go `modernc.org/sqlite` (no CGO needed)\n- **`models.go`** — `Book` struct + validation (title/author required)\n- **`store.go`** — SQLite-backed `Store` with CRUD operations (works with `:memory:`)\n- **`handler.go`** — `net/http` handlers for all endpoints, JSON responses, proper status codes\n- **`main.go`** — CLI entry point with `-addr`/`-db` flags\n- **`handler_test.go`** — 3 integration tests covering the full lifecycle, validation/filtering, and not-found cases\n- **`README.md`** — setup, run, endpoint reference, curl examples\n\nAll endpoints implemented: `GET /health`, `POST/GET /books` (with `?author=` filter), `GET/PUT/DELETE /books/{id}`. Build OK, `go vet` clean, all tests pass.","time":{"start":1788384290841,"end":1788384294458}}}
